# Signup: the happy path, plus what happens when things go wrong.

Test: New user signup shows up on the admin dashboard

  Start with: empty database
  Users: new visitor, admin

  As admin:
    go to users page
    should see "Total users: 0"
    should see "No users yet"

  As new visitor:
    go to signup page
    type "rahim@test.com" in email
    type "Secret123" in password
    click "Sign up"

    backend should receive  POST /api/users
    backend should reply    201 Created
    reply should not contain password

    should see "Welcome, Rahim"
    should see "You have no orders yet"

  As admin:
    reload the page
    should see "Total users: 1"
    should see "rahim@test.com"


Test: Signup with an email that already exists

  Start with: one user "rahim@test.com"

  As new visitor:
    go to signup page
    type "rahim@test.com" in email
    type "Secret123" in password
    click "Sign up"

    backend should receive  POST /api/users
    backend should reply    409 Conflict
    should see "This email is already registered"
    should still be on signup page


Test: Signup with an invalid email is stopped in the browser

  As new visitor:
    go to signup page
    type "abc" in email
    type "Secret123" in password
    click "Sign up"

    should see "Please enter a valid email"
    backend should not receive any request


Test: Signup when the server is down

  As new visitor:
    go to signup page
    when the server fails on POST /api/users
    type "rahim@test.com" in email
    type "Secret123" in password
    click "Sign up"

    should see "Something went wrong, please try again"
    "Sign up" button should be enabled again


Test: Signup while the server is slow shows a loading state

  Start with: empty database

  As new visitor:
    go to signup page
    when the server is slow on POST /api/users by 2 seconds
    type "rahim@test.com" in email
    type "Secret123" in password
    click "Sign up"

    "Sign up" button should be disabled
    should see "Welcome, Rahim"
